{"signature": "{\"text\": \"A reliable calculation method is to write the equation, identify each value with its unit, substitute and calculate, then state the answer with its unit. Be particularly careful to use the vertical change in height, not the distance travelled along a slope. If mass is given in grams, divide by one thousand to convert it into kilograms. Use the value of gravitational field strength supplied in the question. GCSE questions often use ten newtons per kilogram, although the value near Earth's surface is approximately 9.8 newtons per kilogram.\", \"voice\": \"en-NG-AbeoNeural\", \"rate\": \"-4%\", \"eleven\": true}", "duration": 35.892245, "words": [["A", 0.0], ["reliable", 0.151], ["calculation", 0.697], ["method", 1.358], ["is", 1.718], ["to", 1.869], ["write", 1.985], ["the", 2.252], ["equation,", 2.368], ["identify", 3.077], ["each", 3.785], ["value", 4.04], ["with", 4.447], ["its", 4.644], ["unit,", 4.911], ["substitute", 5.306], ["and", 6.107], ["calculate,", 6.293], ["then", 6.943], ["state", 7.198], ["the", 7.535], ["answer", 7.674], ["with", 8.185], ["its", 8.417], ["unit.", 8.626], ["Be", 9.091], ["particularly", 9.288], ["careful", 9.915], ["to", 10.356], ["use", 10.553], ["the", 10.855], ["vertical", 10.983], ["change", 11.505], ["in", 12.005], ["height,", 12.225], ["not", 12.713], ["the", 12.992], ["distance", 13.166], ["travelled", 13.735], ["along", 14.292], ["a", 14.617], ["slope.", 14.698], ["If", 15.232], ["mass", 15.488], ["is", 15.859], ["given", 16.08], ["in", 16.463], ["grams,", 16.649], ["divide", 17.299], ["by", 17.81], ["one", 18.065], ["thousand", 18.321], ["to", 19.098], ["convert", 19.342], ["it", 19.841], ["into", 20.027], ["kilograms.", 20.445], ["Use", 21.362], ["the", 21.687], ["value", 21.827], ["of", 22.21], ["gravitational", 22.361], ["field", 23.22], ["strength", 23.568], ["supplied", 24.056], ["in", 24.683], ["the", 24.834], ["question.", 24.95], ["GCSE", 25.89], ["questions", 26.773], ["often", 27.574], ["u